id: pm-fa9olc
title: Transaction preview refusal should identify a safe relative offending path
description: "During the current all-status tracker intake, pm item mutate --dry-run refused transaction_preview_non_regular_file without identifying which storage entry required repair. The safety boundary is correct and shipped under pm-preview-path-refusal, whose explicit path-redaction policy must remain intact. Improve operator recovery with a bounded tracker-relative category or safe diagnostic coordinate, never an absolute host path or following links. This is a new diagnostic enhancement, not a reopening of the shipped refusal."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 3
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-18T21:52:35.071Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T11:05:53.585Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-19T11:05:52.577Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-19T11:05:52.577Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: A safe bounded diagnostic identifies the relevant storage category or tracker-relative entry without exposing host paths; Non-regular entries remain refused before reading or mutating them; Diagnostics explain how to inspect and repair the entry without requiring force
parent: pm-srns
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Add typed preview_storage coordinates with fixed categories, bounded safe tracker-relative entries, explicit unsafe-name redaction, and inspection/repair guidance. Preserve non-following admission and native filesystem diagnostics."
expected_result: "Operators can identify and repair refused storage without exposing absolute paths or link targets, while unsafe names remain redacted and source data stays unchanged."
actual_result: "Linked160 tests pass, including real links, FIFOs, descriptor races, source snapshots and CLI/MCP parity. The strengthened human-message/next-step privacy file passes27 tests and lint. Complete hosted CI39239473255 proves exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; static quality, TypeScript and Node/Bun tarball acceptance pass. PR1506 carries the implementation and required final review."
